   "k": "final claims text",
   "v": "I found 5 published papers, 1 condition, 1 literature index entry and 5 clinical trials related to Marfan syndrome.⁠1 +11\n\nThere is currently no radical treatment, but early identification, early diagnosis, and early treatment can effectively prolong patients' lives.⁠83 Neonatal Marfan syndrome is especially rare, with severe conditions and a poor prognosis.⁠83 MedGen lists these clinical features: Aortic regurgitation, Arachnodactyly and Astigmatism, Ectopia lentis, Esotropia, Exotropia and Pes planus, Glaucoma, Congestive heart failure, Hypertropia and Micrognathia.⁠3–13 Marfan syndrome and Marfan syndrome.⁠79, 81\n\nWHERE THIS ANSWER COMES FROM\nMarfan syndrome.⁠1\nMarfan syndrome⁠2\nMarfan Syndrome⁠73\nStudies of Heritable Disorders of Connective Tissue⁠74\n[Latest advances in the diagnosis and treatment of Marfan syndrome].⁠75\nComparison of Two Medications Aimed at Slowing Aortic Root Enlargement in Individuals With Marfan Syndrome⁠76\nWhat Is Marfan Syndrome?⁠77\nAngiotensin Converting Enzyme Inhibitors in Marfan Syndrome⁠78\nMarfan syndrome.⁠79\nLosartan Versus Atenolol for the Treatment of Marfan Syndrome⁠80\nShowing 1–10 of 12\n‹ Previous\nPage 1 of 2\nNext ›\nCLINICAL FEATURES MEDGEN LISTS FOR MARFAN SYNDROME\nAortic regurgitation⁠3\nArachnodactyly⁠4\nAstigmatism⁠5\nEctopia lentis⁠6\nEsotropia⁠7\nExotropia⁠8\nPes planus⁠9\nGlaucoma⁠10\nCongestive heart failure⁠11\nHypertropia⁠12\nShowing 1–10 of 70\n‹ Previous\nPage 1 of 7\nNext ›"
  },
